    "ruleType": "detachment-rule",
    "group": "Pantheon of Woe",
    "summary": "Every NECRONS MONSTER unit in your army gains Distortion Fields (Aura): an enemy unit within 6″ of it is unravelling, and attacks aimed at an unravelling unit have their AP improved by 1. When each phase starts, any NECRONS MONSTER unit of yours may take 3 mortal wounds; one that does has a 9″ Distortion Fields range until that phase ends. If your army includes two or more TRANSCENDENT C’TAN units, every one of them must be given Reletavistic Tether.\n\nThe rule also sets out four Necrodermal Binding Abilities, each priced as its own Enhancement:\nSingularity Matrix (45 points; C’TAN SHARD OF THE DECEIVER only) gives that model Lord of Deceit (Aura): whenever your opponent uses a Stratagem on one of their units within 12″ of it, that use costs 1 CP more.\nQuantum Goad (45 points; C’TAN SHARD OF THE NIGHTBRINGER only) means Advancing does not stop that model from declaring a charge that turn.\nAnimus Damper (35 points; C’TAN SHARD OF THE VOID DRAGON only) works once per turn: as the Shooting phase of your opponent begins, pick one enemy VEHICLE unit that the bearer can see; that unit takes a Leadership test, and until the phase ends attacks made by its models get −1 to hit, plus −1 to wound if that test was failed.\nReletavistic Tether (40 points) is for TRANSCENDENT C’TAN models alone: during your turn, whenever that model uses its Transdimensional Displacement ability to make an ingress/advance move, it may stop with every enemy unit more than 6″ away horizontally (rather than more than 8″); if it stops with an enemy unit within 8″, it may not declare a charge until that turn ends.",
